  "reason": "The current best (config_050, acc=0.520) uses transformer aggregation with weighted fusion, scgpt, and imagenet_vit_l. The only other aggregation tested (in config_040) was also transformer with concat fusion, which underperformed. We have no evidence yet about whether avgpool aggregation could match or beat transformer in the multimodal multiprofile setting. config_019 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable comparison to the current best, changing only aggregation from transformer to avgpool. This is the best use of the next experiment because: (1) it directly tests a fundamental architectural choice with minimal confounding, (2) if avgpool performs comparably, it validates a simpler/faster architecture and frees later experiments to explore other dimensions (RNA encoder, image encoder), and (3) if it underperforms, it confirms transformer aggregation is critical and we can focus remaining budget on encoder and profile choices. With 6 experiments left, reducing uncertainty on this core design axis early is more valuable than jumping to a less-tested dimension."
}

